  "source": "GROUND.md §9.4. Gibs: how the pieces of a broken thing fly, settle and go, read by game/scripts/Gibs/GibCatalog.cs (the client only). Which pieces a model breaks into is the model catalogue's (models.json, each entry's gibs: its file and material). Lengths in metres, speeds in m/s, spins in radians a second, times in seconds; [a, b] is a range picked per piece. limits: pieces alive at once (the oldest go first), how near the camera a break shows its pieces (beyond: dust only) and how far it shows at all, and above what share of the cap a break keeps only its bigger pieces. physics: the cheap integrator's numbers (gravity when the caller gives none, drags, when a piece sleeps, how far down its floor is looked for, the longest a piece lives). life: how long a piece rests before it sinks, and the sinking. materials: each piece's bounce and friction, how much it spins, its dust (an effect of fx.json, tinted by colour, a linear RGB) and its sound (sounds.json; a model's own 'break' sound wins). causes: how a blow throws the pieces: push along the blow, spread out from the middle, lift, spin, the dust's size, and a sound that wins over the rest (the hammer's).",
